## Propagating Trace Context Through RabbitMQ Headers

The key is to **inject** the current trace context into message headers on publish and **extract** it on consume, then start a new activity linked to that context.

### Service A (Publisher)

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;
using RabbitMQ.Client;

private static readonly ActivitySource ActivitySource = new("ServiceA.Messaging");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void PublishOrder(OrderEvent order, IModel channel)
{
    using var activity = ActivitySource.StartActivity("OrderEvent publish", ActivityKind.Producer);

    var props = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
    props.Headers ??= new Dictionary<string, object>();

    // Inject current context into message headers
    Propagator.Inject(
        new PropagationContext(activity.Context, Baggage.Current),
        props.Headers,
        (headers, key, value) => headers[key] = value);

    var body = JsonSerializer.SerializeToUtf8Bytes(order);
    channel.BasicPublish(exchange: "orders", routingKey: "", basicProperties: props, body: body);
}
```

### Service B (Consumer)

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using System.Text;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;
using RabbitMQ.Client.Events;

private static readonly ActivitySource ActivitySource = new("ServiceB.Messaging");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void HandleMessage(object sender, BasicDeliverEventArgs ea)
{
    // Extract propagated context from headers
    var parentContext = Propagator.Extract(
        default,
        ea.BasicProperties.Headers,
        (headers, key) =>
        {
            if (headers != null && headers.TryGetValue(key, out var value))
            {
                return new[] { Encoding.UTF8.GetString((byte[])value) };
            }
            return Enumerable.Empty<string>();
        });

    Baggage.Current = parentContext.Baggage;

    // Start a new activity linked to the extracted parent
    using var activity = ActivitySource.StartActivity(
        "OrderEvent consume",
        ActivityKind.Consumer,
        parentContext.ActivityContext);

    // Process the message...
}
```

### OTel SDK Registration (both services)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(tracing => tracing
        .AddSource("ServiceA.Messaging")  // or ServiceB.Messaging
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddOtlpExporter());
```

### Why it works

- **W3C TraceContext** (`traceparent`/`tracestate`) is the default propagator in .NET 8.
- RabbitMQ headers are `IDictionary<string, object>` — values arrive as `byte[]` on the consumer side, hence the `Encoding.UTF8.GetString` cast.
- By passing the extracted `ActivityContext` as the parent when starting the consumer activity, the two spans share the same `TraceId`, giving you a single end-to-end trace in your backend (Jaeger, Tempo, etc.).

> **Tip:** If you're using MassTransit or NServiceBus, this propagation is built-in. The manual approach above is needed only for raw `RabbitMQ.Client` usage.
